pipa: touch mapping — real panel spans, iOS frame placement, zonal Y mirror

The applied path clamped raw touch coordinates to 1079x2399 (the alioth
phone glass), then mapped through the apollo phone-logical 1080x2400 space.
The pipa touch glass covers the panel 1800x2880 (SR/10), so everything past
1079x2399 was crushed onto two lines: half the screen appeared dead.

Replaced the whole normalize with the pipa model:
- clamps to the real glass 1799x2879;
- the iOS frame (1125x2436) is presented as 1080x2338 centered on the panel
  (x 360..1439, y 271..2608, per 0150); touch maps into the frame 1:1;
- the touch zones mirror Y on the left half of the glass (the observed:
  the bottom taps open the top apps on the screen left), the right zone is
  direct;
- the 0187 piecewise Y shear and the fFit/0150 branches are subsumed by the
  zonal mapping and dropped.

Boot-tested: pending.
